nd sets things up for us even before we are born, as explained in the life of the prophet Jeremiah, as Jeremiah 1:5 describes, \u201cBefore I formed you in the belly I knew you, and before you came forth out of the womb I sanctified you; and I ordained you a prophet unto the nations.\u201d\n\nAs Christians, we believe in the providence of God and His hand at work in our lives. \nJoseph believed God had more for him, yet he spent years as a slave and in prison being prepared for his God-given dream destiny.\nAs a shepherd boy, David didn\u2019t dream of being king. Yet, God was spending one-on-one time with him out on the fields, preparing his heart and mind to fight for, protect, and lead His people.\n\nRecognize God\u2019s gentle leading as He prepares our hearts and minds for His plans ahead, even if we don\u2019t realize it now. He\u2019s gently leading and guiding us, and we are following, whether we\u2019re aware or relatively clueless. Be prepared in season and out of season\u2014with great patience. Be still and know that He is God.\n", "author": "Come-mistertallyman", "created": 1788188126923, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Ndmand69", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "God is always preparing you for the great plans He created you for", "last_comment_created": 1788198455877, "content": "<p>\u201cFor we are his workmanship, created in Christ Jesus unto good works, which God has before ordained that we should walk in them.\u201d (Ephesians 2:10)</p>\n<p>God wants you to recognize He has made you with special plans in mind. God is and has been preparing you for this purpose ONLY YOU CAN FULFILL. It\u2019s remarkable how God is at work behind the scenes in our lives, 